1. Scope and definitions

"Covered Material" means the AKC QA Platform source code and other material
distributed under this license, and modifications or derivative works of
that material to the extent protected by applicable law. "Licensor" means
each rights holder granting this license, only for rights that holder controls.
"You" may be an individual, company, developer, or other organization.

"Commercial benefit" includes fees, subscriptions, API charges, advertising,
and substantially equivalent direct or indirect monetization of a restricted
offering described in section 3. Revenue from a product merely tested with
the Covered Material is not, by itself, a restricted offering.

2. Permission

Subject to this license, Licensor grants You a nonexclusive, worldwide,
royalty-free permission to download, copy, study, run, modify, rename,
integrate, and redistribute the Covered Material for commercial and
noncommercial purposes, except for the two restricted uses in section 3.

This expressly permits testing products You lawfully develop, own, operate,
or are authorized to develop, repair, or maintain, including commercial
products, paid SaaS, websites, apps, internal systems, and products under
development. It permits enterprise internal QA, CI/CD and quality workflows,
and internal customization or renaming. Internal modifications need not be
published. Your identity as a QA company does not exclude these permissions.

It also permits incidental QA during genuine authorized product development,
repair, or maintenance for a client, and compensated installation,
configuration, consulting, or integration, when the actual offering is not
one of the restricted uses in section 3. Free learning, research, modification,
and sharing are permitted subject to the same terms.

3. Two restricted uses requiring separate permission

Without a separate prior written license from the relevant rights holder(s),
You may not use the Covered Material or a derivative of it:

(a) to provide to third parties, for commercial benefit, an independent QA
    testing service or QA report service. Independence is determined from
    the actual nature of the offering and its deliverables, rather than
    merely whether QA has a separate invoice line. Genuine incidental
    quality verification within authorized product development, repair,
    or maintenance is not automatically an independent QA service; or

(b) to repackage, sell, license, or operate for commercial benefit an
    externally offered QA product, platform, hosted or managed service,
    API, or substantially equivalent offering that commercializes the
    QA capabilities of the Covered Material or its derivatives. This
    includes selling the repackaged QA tool itself and monetization through
    subscriptions, API fees, advertising, or equivalent arrangements.

Evaluate the principal and substantive deliverables, actual business model,
rights in the tested systems, and the role of the Covered Material together.
Whether You charge a separately named QA fee, use AKC as the primary tool,
keep its name, change its name, split charges, or bundle services is not
alone decisive. Renaming or bundling does not avoid a restricted use, and
being a business or earning revenue does not alone create one.

These restrictions concern commercializing the Covered Material's QA
services or platform capabilities, not all uses connected with business.
Where facts are materially uncertain, identify the uncertainty and seek
clarification from the relevant rights holder(s); uncertainty does not add
a new category of prohibition to this license.

